NAME
       tr - translate, delete or squeeze bytes

SYNOPSIS
       tr [-cCdst] string1 [string2]

DESCRIPTION
       Translate, delete or squeeze bytes. Strings take ranges
       (a-z), classes ([:alpha:]), equivalence classes
       ([=a=]), repeats in string2 ([x*] and [x*n]) and the
       escapes \\ \a \b \f \n \r \t \v \NNN. As in GNU tr, a
       short string2 is padded with its last byte unless -t is
       given.

SEE ALSO
       sh(1)

